VeridianOS: track application font changes without QGuiApplication::fontChanged

GCC reported -Wdeprecated-declarations for QGuiApplication::fontChanged()
("Handle QEvent::ApplicationFontChange instead") in the BreezeDial and
PaintedSymbolItem constructors (style/impl/breezedial.cpp,
style/impl/paintedsymbolitem.cpp), which connected to it to refresh their
cached font metrics.

QGuiApplication::setFont() emits the deprecated signal and, right after,
sends QEvent::ApplicationFontChange to the application object; that is the
only place either happens. Items do not receive that event themselves, so
each item now installs itself as an event filter on qGuiApp and, on
ApplicationFontChange addressed to qGuiApp, refreshes its font metrics and
schedules a repaint exactly as the lambda did. This is the pattern
Kirigami's Units uses for the same purpose. eventFilter() is declared as a
protected override in breezedial.h and paintedsymbolitem.h; it always
passes the event on.

Behaviour is unchanged. A filter on the application object sees every
event of the GUI thread; the added cost per item is one pointer and type
comparison per event.

diff -ru a/style/impl/breezedial.cpp b/style/impl/breezedial.cpp
--- a/style/impl/breezedial.cpp	2026-10-08 17:27:14.670711624 -0400
+++ b/style/impl/breezedial.cpp	2026-10-08 17:27:35.096400361 -0400
@@ -32,17 +32,24 @@
     : QQuickPaintedItem(parent)
     , d_ptr(new BreezeDialPrivate(this))
 {
-    Q_D(BreezeDial);
-    connect(qGuiApp, &QGuiApplication::fontChanged, this, [this, d]() {
-        d->fontMetrics = QFontMetricsF(QGuiApplication::font());
-        update();
-    });
+    // ApplicationFontChange is sent to the application object only
+    qGuiApp->installEventFilter(this);
 }
 
 BreezeDial::~BreezeDial() noexcept
 {
 }
 
+bool BreezeDial::eventFilter(QObject *watched, QEvent *event)
+{
+    if (watched == qGuiApp && event->type() == QEvent::ApplicationFontChange) {
+        Q_D(BreezeDial);
+        d->fontMetrics = QFontMetricsF(QGuiApplication::font());
+        update();
+    }
+    return QQuickPaintedItem::eventFilter(watched, event);
+}
+
 void BreezeDial::paint(QPainter *painter)
 {
     Q_D(BreezeDial);
diff -ru a/style/impl/breezedial.h b/style/impl/breezedial.h
